{"availability":"available","full":"benbalter/emdash-document-revisions","name":"emdash-document-revisions","description":"Document management for EmDash: versioned files stored privately in R2 and served through permission-checked permalinks. A port of WP Document Revisions.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T01:21:28Z","updated":"2026-10-08T05:09:20Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["astro","cloudflare-workers","document-management","emdash","emdash-plugin","r2","revisions","wp-document-revisions"],"demo":"https://wordpress.org/playground/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:00.166Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:00.166Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:00.166Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:35:00.166Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Document management for EmDash. Each document is a series of uploaded files with a revision log, and files are served only through permission-checked links. Think policies, handbooks, board minutes, contracts: files a team keeps updating, where people need the current version, the history of who changed what, and some documents kept private.","It's a TypeScript port of WP Document Revisions, the WordPress plugin, for EmDash on Cloudflare Workers. If you're moving a WordPress site to EmDash, the importer brings your document library along, history and old links included.","Early and unproven. It's been built and tested end to end against EmDash 1.1 in Cloudflare's local runtime, but not yet run on a production Cloudflare deployment. APIs may change before 1.0, and it relies on a few EmDash internals that a future EmDash release could move (see Upgrading). Try it on a test site first, and please report what you find. Not affiliated with EmDash or Cloudflare."],"features":["Versioned documents. Every upload becomes a numbered revision with author, date and note. Restore any earlier revision.","Private storage. Files live in their own R2 bucket and are reachable only through /documents/… links, which check permissions on every request, including Range requests from PDF viewers and media players.","Visibility per document: public, private (Editors, Admins and the author) or password-protected. New documents are private by default, as in WP Document Revisions.","Stable links. /documents/tps-report.pdf always serves the latest file; /documents/tps-report-revision-3.pdf serves revision 3. The dated /documents/2011/08/… form from WordPress works too.","Check-out locking through EmDash's own edit lock. Nobody uploads over someone who's editing."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/benbalter/emdash-document-revisions/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"95028e24bb5941f3caef8eb062ee243407adfab784716d36fcdb9f762a612520","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:00.399Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:35:00.399Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Document management for EmDash. Each document is a series of uploaded files with a revision log, and files are served only through permission-checked links. Think policies, handbooks, board minutes, contracts: files a team keeps updating, where people need the current version, the history of who changed what, and some documents kept private.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/benbalter/emdash-document-revisions/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"No Cloudflare account or login is needed.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/benbalter/emdash-document-revisions/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The rate-limit binding needs no setup beyond its namespaceid, any number unique within your account.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/benbalter/emdash-document-revisions/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"95028e24bb5941f3caef8eb062ee243407adfab784716d36fcdb9f762a612520","sourceUrl":"https://gi